/* book exam traps: Do not confuse piezoresistive with piezoelectric. Piezoresistive changes resistance under strain and works for steady loads; piezoelectric makes charge under stress and cannot hold a steady reading without charge leakage. | The capacitance formula is non-linear in d. A 10 % reduction in gap (d falls to 0.9 d) raises C by about 11 % (1/0.9 = 1.111), not 10 %; a 10 % increase in gap lowers C by about 9.1 %. The relation is non-linear and not symmetric. | A Seebeck emf depends on the temperature difference, not the absolute temperature. A thermocouple still needs a cold junction before it reports absolute temperature. | In VH = RH·I·B/t, the thickness t is in the denominator. Doubling the sheet thickness halves the Hall voltage for the same current and field. | A photovoltaic cell gives an emf; a photoconductive cell changes resistance and needs a bias supply. They are not interchangeable circuits. */
